From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 17:14:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] tccgen: __auto_type drops the top-level qualifiers

"__auto_type c = ci;" with a const int ci kept the const (an assignment
to c warned "assignment of read-only location"); gcc declares a plain int,
as C23's auto does.  The pointee's qualifiers stay.

Fix 101 of the tinycc-os-kernel project (docs/FIX-LOG.md).
---
 tccgen.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tccgen.c b/tccgen.c
index 7284a09..06cad38 100644
--- a/tccgen.c
+++ b/tccgen.c
@@ -9171,7 +9171,7 @@ static void decl_initializer_alloc(CType *type, AttributeDef *ad, int r,
         expr_type(type, expr_eq);
         /* as with typeof, except that arrays and functions decay and
            a bit-field yields its underlying integer type */
-        type->t &= ~(VT_STORAGE | VT_ARRAY | VT_VLA);
+        type->t &= ~(VT_STORAGE | VT_ARRAY | VT_VLA | VT_CONSTANT | VT_VOLATILE);
         if (type->t & VT_BITFIELD)
             type->t &= ~(VT_BITFIELD | (0xfffU << VT_STRUCT_SHIFT));
         if ((type->t & VT_BTYPE) == VT_FUNC)
